### The Lighting window (scene/lighting/LightingPanel.vue). $name is the name of a light entity (data).

lighting-presets = Presets
lighting-preset-studio = Studio
lighting-preset-daylight = Daylight
lighting-preset-evening = Evening
lighting-preset-night = Night
lighting-preset-neutral = Neutral
lighting-maps = Environment map
lighting-map-none = No map
lighting-lights = Lights
lighting-no-lights = The scene has no light.
lighting-intensity = The intensity of { $name }
lighting-ask = Ask the agent to light this
lighting-ask-none = No agent is connected: the agent panel (⌘L) says how to connect one.
lighting-ask-prompt = Light this scene: choose the environment, the exposure, the fog and the lights so that the selected entities look their best. Keep each change small and tell me what you changed.
